{"table":"nodes","ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/scalar.lean_scalar_target","record":{"id":"scalar.lean_scalar_target","kind":"declaration","label":"OAI.SKValue.scalar_value_target","status":"unverified","source_id":"scalar-r2-26-source-formal-targets","locator":"GroundState/MainConclusions.lean:13–15; scalar_value_target","statement":"For every W:BrownianSpace, gamma:OrderParameter and X:R→W.Omega→R, IsMinimizer W gamma and IsDiffusion W gamma X imply ScalarValueConclusion W gamma X, whose full conjunction is Model.lean:106–118.","assumption_ids":["assumptions.value_minimizer","assumptions.value_diffusion"],"evidence_ids":[],"citation_ids":["scalar-r2-26-cite-lean-scalar-target"],"boundary":"The exact SKValue model uses a coefficient on all reals with its stated interval fields, BrownianSpace and its natural filtration. Source inspected; no kernel replay, Comparator acceptance or elaborated dependency extraction is recorded.","declaration":"OAI.SKValue.scalar_value_target"},"usage":{"record_ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/scalar.lean_scalar_target","paper_focus":[],"paper_memberships":[{"stage":"long","subgraph_ref":"sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json/support/0.3.1/69473417dc487cafa5e2e39b3168d2c4a8bffdad2e91b6e486de48f122dda071","roles":["mapped_claim"]},{"stage":"short","subgraph_ref":"sha256:b3fb22a55f09aba18f53cd9bbac859142355ee389bba5aa7bf98d016dc611a43/papers/short.json/support/0.3.1/77f0cf29ab577b42d8caa5b2831ebfb1ca170d4b13c1ef6897cadc8e93c2a834","roles":["recorded_prerequisite"]},{"stage":"expository","subgraph_ref":"sha256:082c1187f897999ee934fa70dbb519221ed1e0aebc169fac91b7211a4a599dc5/papers/expository.json/support/0.3.1/9dd5536bc567fc55efaa864733bf89747cea0268a8a3865dec51ddd8e2a235dd","roles":["recorded_prerequisite"]}],"direct_passages":[{"stage":"long","passage_ref":"sha256:9e0f6d255eb0a116c513a0c11e94d28559f0a429ef365c3137bb4ff3b6a061d6/papers/long.md/sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json/passages/formal-scalar","anchor":"formal-scalar","mapping_ref":"sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json","mapping_field":"claim_ids"}]},"aligned_passages":[{"stage":"long","passage_ref":"sha256:9e0f6d255eb0a116c513a0c11e94d28559f0a429ef365c3137bb4ff3b6a061d6/papers/long.md/sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json/passages/formal-scalar","anchor":"formal-scalar","mapping_ref":"sha256:7588abc48d1c21bb64c366849eaa851938d6acc6b17cf16f89ccf8b87ca26853/papers/long.json","mapping_field":"claim_ids","text":"\n<a id=\"formal-scalar-statement\"></a>\n\n### 12.2 The separate scalar statement\n\nThe second formal statement has three clauses. Given a minimizer and an\nassociated diffusion, it establishes convergence of the finite-spin\nground-state values, a bounded martingale with a spin-valued terminal\nlimit, convergence of the gradient and the value identities. Under the\nsame hypotheses and fixed $0<T<1$, it gives eventual positivity of the\nGaussian normalizers and convergence of the finite coefficient sum.\nThese are the declarations `scalar_value_target` and\n`finite_gaussian_target`. Their caller supplies the same minimizer and\nassociated diffusion. The implementation derives compact-strip bounds\nfrom `sourceStripRegularity` and the unit curvature moment from contact\nfor those objects before applying its fixed-strip helper. Those internal\ninputs are not additional hypotheses of the exported clauses. The\nconvergence clause establishes existence of the finite-spin limit.\n\nThe index match in the Gaussian statement is exact. For\n$\\Delta=T/N$ and $t_j=j\\Delta$, the Euler path uses\n$Z_1,\\ldots,Z_N$ and produces $Y_0,\\ldots,Y_N$.\nThe source normalizer indexed from zero corresponds to manuscript\n$c_1,\\ldots,c_N$; its eventual positivity covers precisely those\nnormalizers. A separate $Z_{N+1}$ performs mean-preserving rounding:\nit enters $B_{N+1}$, not another Euler increment. Thus the finite sum is\n$\\sum_{j=0}^{N}A_jB_{j+1}$ with $A_0=0$, using exactly the displayed\nindex ranges. Total definitions at $N=0$ make no extra mathematical\nclaim about the construction for $N\\ge1$. More explicitly, the\nzero-based formal quantities `coordinate N j`, `rawCoefficient ... j`\nand `normalizer ... j` correspond to $Z_{j+1}$,\n$a(t_j,Y_j)$ and $c_{j+1}$ for $0\\le j<N$. The positivity quantifiers\nare $\\exists N_0\\,\\forall N\\ge N_0\\,\\forall j<N$, simultaneously over\nthe growing mesh, for each already fixed $T$. The extra coordinate\nwith formal index $N$ is $Z_{N+1}$. The formal martingale stops at its\nterminal random variable $U$ for all later times; $U^2=1$ almost surely,\nand the gradient converges to $U$ almost surely and in $L^2$ from below\none. The internal terminal-gradient lemma proves $UX_1=|X_1|$\nwithout requiring $X_1$ to have no atom at zero. That identity is used\ninside the implementation; it is not an extra conjunct of the endpoint. See the [scalar statement][value-type] and its\ncomplete dictionary.\n\n","span":{"start_byte":229424,"end_byte":231840,"start_line":4943,"end_line":4984},"paper_href":"/api/v1/papers/long?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb","reading_href":"/api/v1/papers/reading?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&paper=long&passage=formal-scalar","query_href":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&paper=long&passage=formal-scalar"}],"lenses":{"prerequisites":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&view=arguments&node=scalar.lean_scalar_target&assumptions=true","consumers":"/api/v1/graph?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&view=arguments&node=scalar.lean_scalar_target&direction=consumers&assumptions=true","direct_passages":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&node=scalar.lean_scalar_target&relation=direct","prerequisite_uses":"/api/v1/papers/query?manifest=79bf16ac8ab3a2adf5741ab97b2e4bd813e1c0a1940efbbdf9e35523f00de8bb&node=scalar.lean_scalar_target&relation=prerequisites"},"relations":[{"family":"arguments","id":"field:3500114d0b03aa7443c817d037b63a88ed18a5da17c06ccea7995bebcc5e2b1f","from":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/scalar.lean_scalar_target","to":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/assumptions.value_minimizer","kind":"assumption_ids","semantic_class":"explicit_assumption_reference","derived":true,"owner_ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/scalar.lean_scalar_target","source_field":"assumption_ids"},{"family":"arguments","id":"field:cdc343b7189f759a1f5a3bf2da08fdc21e8ca731f2881c49f94d02d8c4d6f7b6","from":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/scalar.lean_scalar_target","to":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/assumptions.value_diffusion","kind":"assumption_ids","semantic_class":"explicit_assumption_reference","derived":true,"owner_ref":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/scalar.lean_scalar_target","source_field":"assumption_ids"},{"family":"arguments","id":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/edges/%5B%22scalar.formal_scalar_clause%22%2C%22scalar.lean_scalar_target%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","from":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/scalar.formal_scalar_clause","to":"sha256:c941bb8e2efcb2c545fdebbfec6f904193275455192bec48bcb452c5b8ab7f97/nodes/scalar.lean_scalar_target","kind":"formalizes","sem